('boss','game',18,'The assistant is waiting.','A FINALE BUILT ON YOUR COMBOS',"The escape ends at the robot assistant. It charges and throws scissors. Later phases bring showers and reinforcements. Stun it, launch your friend, and land on its head. The moves you've learned become your way through the final fight."),
('audience','audience',16,'For the person next to you.','LOCAL CO-OP FIRST',"We're making this for two people who enjoy solving something together, sharing one keyboard. The prototype runs in a browser. PICO PARK and ibb and obb are useful reference points. Our focus is hair-powered combinations inside one mischievous salon."),
('proof','proof',16,'You can play it today.','THE CURRENT PROTOTYPE',"The playable prototype has four chapters, twelve rooms, saved progress, and a three-phase boss. It starts with learning each haircut, then asks you to combine them under new conditions. Every exit needs both friends."),
('plan','plan',22,'Watch real pairs play.','OUR PROPOSED NEXT STEP',"Next, we want twenty pairs to play without us explaining the puzzles. Can they learn the first combo? Where do they get stuck? Do they choose another room? Our proposed twelve-week plan starts with those tests, then clearer tutorials, room and audio polish, accessibility, and release preparation."),
('budget','budget',18,'A focused production plan.','PROPOSED · USD',"We estimate seventeen thousand two hundred US dollars for that twelve-week plan. It covers our time, commissioned art and audio, launch costs, and a twenty-percent buffer. The immediate help we're looking for is playtesters and mentoring."),
